PromptDialogue: {
	MushroomMonarch: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: Woah! Big mushroom! And it's moving... I guess that's not too weird for this world.
			Eridani: The fungi of this world are truly strange... Best not to underestimate this foe.
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: It's flying away! Guess we won...? I'll take it.
			Eridani: The Monarch flees. A temporary victory, but a victory nonetheless.
		}
	}

	FeudalFungus: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: Glowing mushroom royalty. Of course that's a thing. Those spores look hazardous, though.
			Eridani: The counterpart to the red monarch. I suspect those luminescent spores carry deleterious properties.
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: It's retreating. A glowing coward, but at least it's gone.
			Eridani: The Feudal Fungus escapes. It will return, but we have bought ourselves time.
		}
	}

	GripsOfChaos: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: Two giant icky hands? Who made these? They don't look friendly.
			Eridani: I can sense chaotic energy eminating from those Grips. Stay on your toes.
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: Hands off! ...Okay, I'll stop. They're down.
			Eridani: A formidable foe, but we prevailed through careful positioning. Though I doubt this is the last we'll see of such chaotic forces.
		}
	}

	TruffleToad: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: A mushroom frog. It glows. Terraria is weird, but I'm starting to enjoy it.
			Eridani: That toad seems agitated. Do not let its diminutive, cute appearance fool you.
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: The toad has croaked. ...I'll see myself out now.
			Eridani: The Truffle Toad is no more. Its agility was noteworthy, but ultimately insufficient.
		}
	}

	Broodmother: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: A real dragon! Okay, this is awesome. ...Please don't burn me to a crisp.
			Eridani: The Broodmother of the Inferno. A pyrogenic reptile of considerable power. Its flames will be lethal.
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: The Broodmother is down! I knew we could do it. ...I won't ask about the burn marks.
			Eridani: The Broodmother is defeated. Its flames have been extinguished. A significant threat neutralized.
		}
	}

	HydraBody: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: One head, two heads... how many are there?! This is getting out of hand.
			Eridani: The Hydra. Each head represents a separate threat. Focus on one at a time.
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: How many heads was that? I lost count. At least they're all gone now.
			Eridani: The Hydra's heads have ceased moving. A well‑fought victory.
		}
	}

	SubzeroSerpent: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: An icy serpent?! Beautiful but probably lethal. Don't get too close.
			Eridani: Subzero Serpent. Its frostfire breath is no joke; maintain distance when possible.
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: That snake just got iced. I'm on a roll today.
			Eridani: The Subzero Serpent is vanquished. Perhaps the tundra will be a little safer to explore now.
		}
	}

	Djinn: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: A genie! Can I get three wishes? No? Just sand and punches?
			Eridani: The Desert Djinn commands the sands themselves. Do not let it control the battlefield.
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: No wishes, but we got loot. I'll take that as a consolation prize.
			Eridani: The Djinn returns to its lamp. The sands are calm once more.
		}
	}

	Sagittarius: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: A robot horse that shoots lasers. Sure, why not. This world keeps surprising me.
			Eridani: A Fulgurian construct, but the Void's influence seems to have taken hold. Proceed with caution.
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: Robot horse is down for the count. 'Extensive damage'? Yeah, no kidding.
			Eridani: Sagittarius decommissioned. It is now little more than scrap.
		}
	}

	Anubis: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: Anubis wants to test us. He said he won't hold back. Let's hope we got this...
			Eridani: Anubis, our ally, now our sparring partner. He seeks to gauge our strength. Do not disappoint.
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: He says we did good. Phew! That was tense, but guess in the end he was all bark, no bite.
			Eridani: Anubis acknowledges our strength. It seems we're ready for whatever might come our way next.
		}
	}

	Athena: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: Oh geez, maybe beating up those Seraphs wasn't a great idea... Get ready for a fight!
			Eridani: It seems our trespassing here didn't go unnoticed... Now we have the Seraph's Queen to contend with.
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: Hah! We showed her! Leaving us alone is the right call.
			Eridani: Athena relents. Seems even she was impressed with your strength. Perhaps amends can be made.
		}
	}

	Greed: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: A giant worm covered in gold. Tacky AND deadly. That's quite the combination.
			Eridani: Greed, the Gilded Glutton. It hoards treasure and despises intruders. A predictable motivation.
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: It burrowed away. Guess we beat it enough for now.
			Eridani: Greed retreats into the stone. The creature lives, but so do we.
		}
	}

	Rajah: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: Woah, that's one big bunny! And MAN does it seem mad.
			Eridani: Rajah Rabbit, the Pouncing Punisher. He seeks justice, but what did we do to attract his ire?

			Murderer: {
				Asphodene: He called you a murderer. {0}, what did you DO?
				Eridani: ...I see. This is no spar. He genuinely despises us. His anger is not without cause.
			}
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: He's flying away... With his ears... As propellers... This world never ceases to impress.
			Eridani: We've bested the Pouncing Punisher, but still, his anger was rather unsettling.

			Murderer: {
				Asphodene: He's gone, but he swore vengeance. Perhaps we should reconsider our choices here...
				Eridani: He retreats with hatred in his eyes. This is not over. We will face him again.
			}
		}
	}

	ForsakenAnubis: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: This guy's got some nerve thinking we aren't ready. This new form of his won't stop us! Let's show him!
			Eridani: The Forsaken Judge rises. He is testing whether we are ready for what lies locked away. Let's prove ourselves ready.
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: You certainly did do good! That was quite the showdown. Let's see what he wants.
			Eridani: A well earned victory. A strategy meeting would indeed be wise. Let's go speak with him.
		}
	}

	AthenaA: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: Athena's not done?! She's going all out for 'one last fight', huh? We'll just have to do the same!
			Eridani: Athena's determined to not lose again... She won't go down as easilly as last time. Be on your guard. The very winds are against us.
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: That's one angry harpy! But she mentioned dark forces waking up... ominous. We'll have to watch our back.
			Eridani: Athena warns of chaotic forces stirring. Who could this 'he' be that she referred to?
		}
	}

	GreedA: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: Greed is back and way stronger! Though I'm afraid our lives aren't for the taking!
			Eridani: Worm King Greed. The glutton has grown. It threatens to consume our very lives.
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: It fled again. Still angry, but at least it's gone for now.
			Eridani: The Worm King escapes. Greed never truly dies; it only hibernates.
		}
	}

	EquinoxWorms: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: The Equinox Worms... they said this would be a test. Here we go.
			Eridani: Daybringer and Nightcrawler. They honor us with a trial of strength. Let us not disappoint.
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: They're fading away. Guess we passed their test after all.
			Eridani: The Equinox Worms dissolve. Seems we've been judged as worthy.
		}
	}

	SistersOfDiscord: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: Ashe and Haruka. They've heard about us. This might be personal.
			Eridani: The Sisters of Discord. Fire and steel, and they want revenge for some past slight.
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: They're retreating. 'Someone has to tell dad'? Who's their dad? I'm curious now.
			Eridani: Ashe and Haruka withdraw. They underestimated our capabilities. Though their father might be someone to worry about.
		}
	}

	YamataBody: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: Seven heads. And it won't stop screaming. Great. Just great.
			Eridani: Yamata, the Dread Nightmare. Massive ego, massive venom. Avoid its breath at all costs.
		}

		Defeat: {
			NotExpert: {
				Asphodene: It's down, but it's already bragging. 'I went easy on ya!' Sure you did.
				Eridani: Yamata's body falls, but something isn't right. I think it might be serious about having gone easy on us...
			}

			Expert: {
				Asphodene: Hah! That hydra wasn't so bad. ...Wait, something doesn't seem right.
				Eridani: Yamata's form collapses, and yet...the air's gone stiff. I detect a deleterious power surge. Brace yourself.
			}
		}
	}

	YamataABody: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: Oh gosh! Seven heads wasn't enough?! Now it's even bigger and angrier. We're in trouble.
			Eridani: So this is Yamata's power has awakened to its fullest. This is its true form – do not falter.
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: It's retreating, still angry. Quite the nerve to be calling us a cheater though. Whatever, we won.
			Eridani: Yamata flees in rage. It will return, but we have proven ourselves today.
		}
	}

	Akuma: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: A fire wyvern that keeps calling us 'kid'. Rude AND deadly. Typical.
			Eridani: Akuma, the Draconian Demon. Head‑on assault or nothing. There is no trickery here.
		}

		Defeat: {
			NotExpert: {
				Asphodene: It dissolved into embers. 'Come back when you're better.' Modest, aren't you?
				Eridani: Akuma's soul remains. The Draconian Demon is not truly dead – merely dispersed.
			}

			Expert: {
				Asphodene: It's dissolving... Did we win? Wait, something's happening...
				Eridani: Akuma's form scatters, yet its essence lingers. No, wait... I sense a power surge building.
			}
		}
	}

	AkumaA: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: It's not over?! The wyvern just got WAY hotter. We really did fan the flames...! This is bad.
			Eridani: This must be Akuma's true, awakened, power. The air temperature is rising dramatically – stay mobile.
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: Finally! It admits we won fair and square. Took long enough.
			Eridani: Akuma concedes defeat. There is a hint of respect in its tone. A grudging honor.
		}
	}

	Zero: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: A floating machine with orbiting weapons. It's speaking in code. Creepy.
			Eridani: Zero. A Doomsday Construct. Its weapons will unleash a relentless assault. Get to cover! Quick!
		}

		Defeat: {
			NotExpert: {
				Asphodene: Zero is down. Though it seems like it was trying to do something at the end there... Maybe we're lucky it malfunctioned.
				Eridani: The construct falls, but its 'Doomsday Protocol' has me worried. We may be lucky it failed to utilize it.
			}
		}
	}

	ZeroProtocol: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: Woah! It just tossed its physical body?! This 'Doomsday Protocol' is no joke! We're fighting a living glitch now.
			Eridani: Tossing away the Zero Unit. Now, we're fighting something else entirely. Its become much more mobile now. Don't let it catch you!
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: A distress signal? Now who could THAT thing be calling for help?! I'm not sure I like that ominous rift either...
			Eridani: Letting that machine get out its distress signal may prove disasterous. I believe the Void's master may be on our horizon.
		}
	}

	SupremeRajah: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: This guy again?! Talk about a power up! But we can't let this bunny be the end of us.
			Eridani: The Champion of the Innocent. This is his true power. We won't win this so easilly.

			Murderer: {
				Asphodene: He's even angrier. 'Murderer' again. We really messed up, didn't we?
				Eridani: No forgiveness. Only vengeance. He will not stop until justice is served.
			}
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: He stopped? Wow, he wants us to take his place? {0}, he's serious.
			Eridani: The Champion passes his duty to us. 'Be the one the innocent can look to.' A heavy responsibility.
		}
	}

	Shen: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: That's... both Yamata AND Akuma. Combined. We're doomed...
			Eridani: Shen Doragon, the Discordian Doomsayer. The true test of our abilities.
		}

		Defeat: {
			Expert: {
				Asphodene: Phew... That was a tough one! Wait a minute... What's happening?
				Eridani: The Doomsayer falls. No, wait. This isn't over, is it? I sense lingering energy.
			}

			NotExpert: {
				Asphodene: Phew... That was a tough one! Wait... 'true power'? You're telling me that wasn't all he had?!
				Eridani: To think that wasn't all that dragon had... I'd be frightened to see what its capable of if it went all out.
			}
		}
	}

	ShenA: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: That wasn't even their final form?! This guy just won't quit!
			Eridani: He is right. We should have anticipated this. The test continues.
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: It's splitting apart! And they're blaming each other. Classic villain teamwork.
			Eridani: Shen Doragon's fusion collapses. 'You will face our fury again.' A cycle without end.
		}
	}

	InfinityZero: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: That's one huge machine... Is this what that distress signal called?! And now its locked onto us. We might be in for it...
			Eridani: A mechanical construct of immense power. This must be what that distress signal was sent to... Get ready.
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: Who the heck was that?! 'Won't be so forgiving'? No way that guys tougher than that mechanical monster, right...?
			Eridani: We're lucky it left so easilly... Its power was off the charts. 'Next time, I won't be so forgiving.' A warning for the future.
		}
	}

	SoulOfCthulhu: {
		Seen: {
			Asphodene: A ship's wheel with a face? And I hear whispers... 'leave'... creepy.
			Eridani: The Soul of Cthulhu. Ancient, malevolent, and now awake. We must be cautious.
		}

		Defeat: {
			Asphodene: It exploded while cursing us. 'By the name of Azathoth!' ...Should we be worried?
			Eridani: Cthulhu's wrath is spent. But his curse shouldn't be taken lightly. This may not be the end... Greater forces may still be at play.
		}
	}
}
